  "final_answer": "**Cause:** `suggestions.ts` called `POST /api/recommend`, and the Python backend has no route at that address. The only recommendation route is `/colleges/recommend`. `app.py` mounts the router under `/api`, so the real address is `/api/colleges/recommend`.\n\nA second mismatch was hiding behind the 404. The backend's `RecommendRequest` requires a `student_profile` field, and the website was sending `{student_id, answers}` at the top level. Fixing only the address would have turned the 404 into a 422 error.\n\n**Fix:** I changed both fetch calls in `suggestions.ts`, in `generateSuggestedColleges` and `generateSuggestedCollegesFromAnswers`:\n- The address is now `/api/colleges/recommend`.\n- The body is now `{ student_profile: { student_id, answers } }`, which is the shape the backend reads (`student_profile.get(\"answers\")`).\n\nI didn't add a second `/recommend` route to the backend, so there is still exactly one recommendation route. `tests/check_recommend.py` now passes all its checks (address exists, one route, `student_profile` sent). I didn't run the real backend or the website.\n\n**Files changed (exactly one):**\n- `client/src/services/college/suggestions.ts`",
